      "title": "Audio languages per title — ${language:text}",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Every film in Radarr and the audio languages its file carries, straight from Radarr's own\nnaming (no translation table here).\n\nFILTERING BY LANGUAGE: use the `Audio language` picker at the top of the dashboard, which is\nnamed in this panel's title. Pick Spanish and you get every film whose file has a Spanish\ntrack, whatever else it also has — \"English, Spanish\" included — and nothing that lacks it.\nThat works because underneath, a film is one series per language; the grouping folds it back\ninto one row.\n\nThe column funnel deliberately does NOT appear on the language column: it can only offer whole\ncell values, so it would list \"Italian, Spanish\" and never a plain \"Spanish\".\n\nThree tiers elsewhere, in the blue/green/orange the quality columns above already use.\nCodec: blue is lossless or object-based, green is lossy at a high bitrate, orange is basic.\nLangs: blue is a real choice of audio, green is a couple, plain text is take it or leave it.\nQuality keeps the exact mapping from \"Stuck on a bad quality\".",
